# Spotify Web API

- **OpenAPI**: Use https://developer.spotify.com/reference/web-api/open-api-schema.yaml for paths, params, and response fields. Do not guess.
- **Auth**: Authorization Code flow on the server (secure backend). Never Implicit Grant. Never expose Client Secret client-side.
- **Redirect URIs**: HTTPS in production; `http://127.0.0.1` only for local dev. Never `localhost` or wildcards.
- **Scopes**: Request minimum scopes only (`user-modify-playback-state`, `user-read-playback-state`, `playlist-read-private`).
- **Tokens**: Encrypt at rest; refresh access tokens; on refresh failure (`invalid_grant`) require re-authorization.
- **Rate limits**: On 429, honor `Retry-After` header and JSON `retryAfter`; use exponential backoff on repeated 429s; never retry in tight loops.
- **Endpoints**: Use `/playlists/{id}/items` not `/tracks`. Do not call `/artists/{id}/top-tracks` (403 in dev mode) — use `/search?q=artist:{name}&type=track` instead.
- **Errors**: Parse Spotify error JSON and surface meaningful messages to the host.
- **Terms**: Attribute playback to Spotify; cache only what sync needs; do not use API data for ML training.
